Create two compound indexes on the collection in the sample DB sample_customer_360_06:
1) { customerId: 1, timestamp: -1 }
2) { channel: 1, timestamp: -1 }
These can be created via Mongoose schema.index() or the mongo shell createIndex commands.

Create indexes from application startup using Mongoose: e.g.
const historySchema = new Schema({ customerId: String, channel: String, timestamp: Date, ... });
historySchema.index({ customerId: 1, timestamp: -1 });
historySchema.index({ channel: 1, timestamp: -1 });
const History = mongoose.model('History', historySchema);
await History.createIndexes();
Alternatively use the mongo shell: db.history.createIndex({ customerId: 1, timestamp: -1 }) and db.history.createIndex({ channel: 1, timestamp: -1 }).
